course: dictionary
lesson: 2554
title: Dehydration: when your body runs low on water
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dehydration is a noun. It means your body does not have enough water. «Dehydration means losing too much water and salts.» You lose water when you sweat, go to the toilet and breathe out, so you need to drink to replace it.
explain: Read the signs in the sentence: a dry mouth, little or dark wee, no tears, dizziness and tiredness. «Even mild dehydration can cause headaches, tiredness and poor concentration.» Mild means not very strong, so you can feel poorly before you are seriously ill.
explain: The word has a second meaning in science and cooking. There, dehydration means removing water from something on purpose, like drying fruit. Check the words around it to see which meaning fits: is the sentence about a person who is ill, or about food being dried?
fact: Dehydration is a noun. It means not having enough water in your body.
fact: You can be dehydrated before you feel thirsty, so do not wait until you are thirsty to drink.
fact: To prevent dehydration, drink water on hot days and during sport.
fact: To «suffer from dehydration» means to feel unwell because your body is short of water.
fact: In cooking and science, dehydration means removing water, as when grapes become raisins.
exercise: «Dehydration means losing too much water and salts.» What does dehydration mean? | Losing your appetite for food | Having too much water in your body | A hot, sunny day at the beach | *Not having enough water in your body
exercise: Which is a sign of dehydration? | Cold hands after swimming | *A dry mouth and dizziness | Feeling full after a big dinner | Laughing a lot at a funny film
exercise: In science and cooking, what does dehydration mean? | Cooking food in very hot water | Adding salt to make food tasty | Keeping a drink cold in the fridge | *Removing water from something, like drying fruit
test: Can you be dehydrated before you feel thirsty? | *Yes, so do not wait until you feel thirsty | No, thirst always comes first | Only after eating fruit | Only if you are lost in a desert
test: Which problems can even mild dehydration cause? | Better eyesight and taller growth | *Headaches, tiredness and poor concentration | Strong muscles and fast running | Sunburn and itchy skin
exam: The runner had to drink plenty of water to ___ dehydration during the race. | *prevent | invent | enjoy | forget
